Hi Managers
            Thanks for all the replies and to HP services . When you
telnet to a host it reads the /etc/gettydefs file.  I was on the right
track , i just commented the line for console in /etc/gettydefs , what
needs to be done is in /etc/gettydefs make a copy of the console entry
and comment that , in the first line change to default and remove the
whatever u  dont want to see when u telnet to a host example n%v for
Tru64 version and (%h) for hostname.
 
 
default# B9600 HUPCL CS8 CLOCAL IXON OPOST ONLCR # B9600 SANE IXANY TAB3
CLOCAL #\r\n\r  %t\r\n\r\n\rlogin: #console
 
#console# B9600 HUPCL CS8 CLOCAL IXON OPOST ONLCR # B9600 SANE IXANY
TAB3 CLOCAL #\r\n\r\n%v (%h) %t\r\n\r\n\rlogin: #console

        
 
Regards





