Thank you to everyone who responded.  I had already had the NVRAM variable os_type set to UNIX and was booting from the SRM
Console.  Kurt A. Ludwig supplied the missing piece to the puzzle when he said to set SRM_BOOT to ON.  This was done as follows:

	>>> edit nvram
	# 10 set SRM_BOOT ON
	# exit
	>>>

I can now boot the Tru64 Unix 4.0g CD without it crashing.  Thank you all again!

Mark


