        ./usr/var/cluster/members/member0/spool/cron/crontabs/.new..root:
                its origin can not be identified.
 
This patch will not be installed.
 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

	Our procedure calls for the restoration of the crontab directory,
which includes this file, after the OS load.  It appears that the failure of
this patch, or one of its dependent patches, causes the /sbin/loader file
not to be updated and it is no longer compatible with this library.

	The solution is going to be either to load the patch kit before we
restore the spool directory, or to baseline the patch kit to fix the install
problem.


