I have installed Matlab Release 13 on an ES40 running Tru64 5.1a.  The 
system has 4.5 GB of memory with 8.4 GB of swap space in "eager" mode. 
 When my Matlab users attempt to run their scripts, an "out of memory" 
error occurs in Matlab.  After reading a technical bulletin on the 
Mathworks support site, I am given to understand that this occurs when 
large martrixes are loaded in to virtual memory they must be loaded into 
contiguous space in the virtual memory.  If virtual memory does not have 
enough contiguous space to load the matrix, an "out of memory" error 
occurs in Matlab.

Is there anyone out there that runs Matlab under Tru64 UNIX?  Have you 
had similar problems?  Are there any solutions?

