Couple of good pointers,

Firstly SNMP,

If you only need to know how many pages are printed on a HP LaserJet
(not who printed what etc), the easiest way would probably be to ask the
printer itself via SNMP. I believe that the OID you are looking for is
1.3.6.1.2.1.43.10.2.1.4.1.1.
You can then query it using (for example)
  snmp_request <printer IP> public get 1.3.6.1.2.1.43.10.2.1.4.1.1
or some other tool for sending SNMP queries.


Otherwise, I think you want to take a look at the 'af' entry in
/etc/printcap.


Hope this is of any help, and good luck!

/Martin Adolfsson

And also several people suggested http://www.lprng.org/

Which is an lp replacement which includes a filter for getting such info. 
 This would have been my chosen route, but unfortunately I have been 
unable to download and untar / gzip the install files.

I will probably look at the SNMP idea in more detail, but in the mean 
time I have hooked something into the database (Universe) print driver 
which will be adequate for now.

Thanks for the responses.

Bryan Mills.


