Fantastic!  I received several very helpful responses to my question =
about getting the client IP address from the shell during a telnet or =
ssh session.  The list of respondents is long so to keep things short =
I'll just say thanks to everyone who replied.

The simplest solution that I received from several people was to use the =
who -m command and pipe it through awk and sed.

#!/bin/sh
client_addr=3D`who -m | awk '{ printf $NF }' |  sed 's/[()]//g'`

Thanks again!

